{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"tm1637-display","name":"4-digit display (TM1637)","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"The red 4-digit 7-segment display with a colon (a clock display) on a TM1637 chip: two wires, CLK and DIO. Includes TM1637Display.h. The part decodes the real TM1637 signals bit by bit.","category":"Displays","needsApp":"0.3.0","code":"// TM1637: a two-wire chip (not I2C, though it looks like it). A transfer starts when DIO falls while\n// CLK is high and ends when DIO rises while CLK is high; in between, each byte goes out least\n// significant bit first, a bit taken on each rising CLK, then a ninth clock for the chip's ACK.\n// Commands: 0x40 \"data, auto increment\" (0x44: fixed address), 0xC0 + n \"start at digit n\" followed\n// by the digits' segments, 0x80-0x8F display control (0x08 = on, 0-7 = brightness).\nbench.device('tm1637', (part) => {\n  const screen = part.screen('digits');\n  const segs = [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0];\n  let clk = 1, dio = 1, inFrame = false, bits = 0, byte = 0, frameBytes = [];\n  let on = false, bright = 7, autoInc = true, powered = false, frames = 0, dirty = true;\n\n  const takeFrame = (f) => {\n    if (!f.length) return;\n    frames++;\n    const c = f[0];\n    if ((c & 0xc0) === 0x40) autoInc = (c & 0x04) === 0;\n    else if ((c & 0xc0) === 0xc0) {\n      let a = c & 0x07;\n      for (const s of f.slice(1)) { if (a < 6) segs[a] = s; if (autoInc) a++; }\n    } else if ((c & 0xc0) === 0x80) { on = (c & 0x08) !== 0; bright = c & 0x07; }\n    dirty = true;\n  };\n  const edge = (pin, lv) => {\n    if (pin === 'CLK') {\n      if (lv && !clk && inFrame) {\n        if (bits < 8) { byte |= (dio ? 1 : 0) << bits; bits++; }\n        else { frameBytes.push(byte); byte = 0; bits = 0; } // (the ninth clock: the ACK)\n      }\n      clk = lv;\n    } else if (pin === 'DIO') {\n      if (clk && dio && !lv) { inFrame = true; bits = 0; byte = 0; frameBytes = []; } // start\n      else if (clk && !dio && lv && inFrame) { inFrame = false; if (bits === 8) frameBytes.push(byte); takeFrame(frameBytes); } // stop\n      dio = lv;\n    }\n  };\n\n  // the screen: 4 digits (6 x 11 dots each) and a colon\n  const X = [0, 8, 18, 26];\n  const SEGS = {\n    a: [[1, 0], [2, 0], [3, 0], [4, 0]], b: [[5, 1], [5, 2], [5, 3], [5, 4]], c: [[5, 6], [5, 7], [5, 8], [5, 9]],\n    d: [[1, 10], [2, 10], [3, 10], [4, 10]], e: [[0, 6], [0, 7], [0, 8], [0, 9]], f: [[0, 1], [0, 2], [0, 3], [0, 4]], g: [[1, 5], [2, 5], [3, 5], [4, 5]],\n  };\n  const draw = () => {\n    const lit = powered && on;\n    const k = 0.35 + 0.65 * ((bright + 1) / 8);\n    const onCol = `rgb(${Math.round(255 * k)},${Math.round(42 * k)},${Math.round(26 * k)})`, offCol = '#2a0d0c', bg = '#121214';\n    screen.fill(bg);\n    for (let d = 0; d < 4; d++) {\n      const s = segs[d];\n      'abcdefg'.split('').forEach((name, i) => {\n        for (const [x, y] of SEGS[name]) screen.set(X[d] + x, y + 1, lit && (s >> i) & 1 ? onCol : offCol);\n      });\n    }\n    const colon = lit && (segs[1] & 0x80);\n    screen.set(16, 4, colon ? onCol : offCol);\n    screen.set(16, 8, colon ? onCol : offCol);\n  };\n  return {\n    edges(events) {\n      for (const [pin, lv] of events) edge(pin, lv);\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\n      const now = v >= 3;\n      if (now !== powered) {\n        powered = now;\n        if (!now) { segs.fill(0); on = false; }\n        dirty = true;\n      }\n      if (powered) { io.drive('CLK', v, 0); io.drive('DIO', v, 0); } // (its pull-ups)\n      // (levels now, for boards that change pins without reporting every change)\n      const c = io.level('CLK'), d = io.level('DIO');\n      if (c !== null && c !== clk) edge('CLK', c);\n      if (d !== null && d !== dio) edge('DIO', d);\n      if (dirty) { draw(); dirty = false; }\n      let litSegs = 0;\n      for (const s of segs.slice(0, 4)) for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) litSegs += (s >> i) & 1;\n      io.draw(powered ? 0.003 + (on ? litSegs * 0.002 * ((bright + 1) / 8) : 0) : 0);\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\n      return [on ? `on, brightness ${bright}, ${frames} transfers` : 'off (send it a brightness: setBrightness)'];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"TM1637Display.h":{"classes":["TM1637Display"],"exports":["SEG_A","SEG_B","SEG_C","SEG_D","SEG_E","SEG_F","SEG_G","SEG_DP"],"code":"// TM1637Display.h (Avishay Orpaz's library): setBrightness(), setSegments(), clear(),\n// showNumberDec(), showNumberDecEx(), showNumberHexEx(), encodeDigit(). It talks to the chip the way\n// the real one does: start, bytes least significant bit first with a clock for each bit, stop.\nconst SEG_A = 0x01, SEG_B = 0x02, SEG_C = 0x04, SEG_D = 0x08, SEG_E = 0x10, SEG_F = 0x20, SEG_G = 0x40, SEG_DP = 0x80;\nconst TM_DIGITS = [0x3f, 0x06, 0x5b, 0x4f, 0x66, 0x6d, 0x7d, 0x07, 0x7f, 0x6f, 0x77, 0x7c, 0x39, 0x5e, 0x79, 0x71];\n\nclass TM1637Display {\n  constructor(clk, dio, bitDelay = 100) {\n    this.clk = clk;\n    this.dio = dio;\n    this.brightness = 0x0f;\n    pinMode(clk, OUTPUT);\n    pinMode(dio, OUTPUT);\n    digitalWrite(clk, HIGH);\n    digitalWrite(dio, HIGH);\n  }\n  setBrightness(b, on = true) { this.brightness = (b & 0x07) | (on ? 0x08 : 0x00); }\n  start() {\n    digitalWrite(this.dio, HIGH);\n    digitalWrite(this.clk, HIGH);\n    digitalWrite(this.dio, LOW);\n  }\n  stop() {\n    digitalWrite(this.clk, LOW);\n    digitalWrite(this.dio, LOW);\n    digitalWrite(this.clk, HIGH);\n    digitalWrite(this.dio, HIGH);\n  }\n  writeByte(b) {\n    for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) {\n      digitalWrite(this.clk, LOW);\n      digitalWrite(this.dio, (b >> i) & 1);\n      digitalWrite(this.clk, HIGH);\n    }\n    // the ninth clock: the chip answers (ACK)\n    digitalWrite(this.clk, LOW);\n    digitalWrite(this.dio, HIGH);\n    digitalWrite(this.clk, HIGH);\n    digitalWrite(this.clk, LOW);\n    return true;\n  }\n  setSegments(segments, length = 4, pos = 0) {\n    this.start();\n    this.writeByte(0x40); // data, auto increment\n    this.stop();\n    this.start();\n    this.writeByte(0xc0 + (pos & 0x03));\n    for (let k = 0; k < length; k++) this.writeByte(segments[k] ?? 0);\n    this.stop();\n    this.start();\n    this.writeByte(0x80 + (this.brightness & 0x0f));\n    this.stop();\n  }\n  clear() { this.setSegments([0, 0, 0, 0]); }\n  encodeDigit(d) { return TM_DIGITS[d & 0x0f]; }\n  showNumberDec(num, leadingZero = false, length = 4, pos = 0) {\n    this.showNumberDecEx(num, 0, leadingZero, length, pos);\n  }\n  showNumberDecEx(num, dots = 0, leadingZero = false, length = 4, pos = 0) {\n    this.showNumberBaseEx(num < 0 ? -10 : 10, num < 0 ? -num : num, dots, leadingZero, length, pos);\n  }\n  showNumberHexEx(num, dots = 0, leadingZero = false, length = 4, pos = 0) {\n    this.showNumberBaseEx(16, num, dots, leadingZero, length, pos);\n  }\n  showNumberBaseEx(base, num, dots, leadingZero, length, pos) {\n    const negative = base < 0;\n    if (negative) base = -base;\n    num = Math.trunc(num);\n    const digits = [0, 0, 0, 0];\n    if (num === 0 && !leadingZero) {\n      for (let i = 0; i < length - 1; i++) digits[i] = 0;\n      digits[length - 1] = TM_DIGITS[0];\n    } else {\n      for (let i = length - 1; i >= 0; --i) {\n        const d = num % base;\n        if (d === 0 && num === 0 && !leadingZero) digits[i] = 0;\n        else digits[i] = TM_DIGITS[d];\n        if (d === 0 && num === 0 && negative) { digits[i] = SEG_G; break; }\n        num = Math.floor(num / base);\n      }\n    }\n    if (dots) for (let i = 0; i < length; i++) { if (dots & 0x80) digits[i] |= 0x80; dots <<= 1; }\n    this.setSegments(digits, length, pos);\n  }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"tm1637","name":"4-digit display (TM1637)","description":"CLK and DIO to any two pins, VCC (3.3-5 V), GND. TM1637Display display(CLK, DIO); display.setBrightness(5); display.showNumberDec(1234); The colon is the top bit of the second digit (showNumberDecEx(1234, 0b01000000)).","swatch":"#1d4fb8","mass":10,"shape":[{"box":[4.2,0.16,2.4],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1d4fb8"},{"box":[3.9,0.6,1.9],"at":[0,0.46,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"screen":{"id":"digits","size":[3.7,1.6],"px":[32,13],"mode":"pixels","on":"#ff2a1a","off":"#2a0d0c","bg":"#121214","dots":false},"at":[0,0.765,0]}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["CLK","DIO","VCC","GND"],"at":[-2.4,0,-0.381],"dir":"z","kinds":{"CLK":"in","DIO":"in","VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5},"CLK":{"pulled":"up"},"DIO":{"pulled":"up"}}}],"device":"tm1637"}],"examples":[{"name":"Counting clock","description":"A TM1637 showing minutes and seconds since the start, with the colon blinking.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Counting clock","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-5,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"disp","type":"tm1637-display/tm1637","name":"Display","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[5,0,1],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"disp","pin":"CLK"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP3"},"b":{"uid":"disp","pin":"DIO"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"disp","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"disp","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Minutes and seconds since the start, the colon blinking every second.\n#include <TM1637Display.h>\n\n#define CLK 2\n#define DIO 3\n\nTM1637Display display(CLK, DIO);\n\nvoid setup() {\n  display.setBrightness(5);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  int s = millis() / 1000;\n  int minutes = s / 60;\n  int seconds = s % 60;\n  int shown = minutes * 100 + seconds;      // mm:ss as one number\n  int half = millis() / 500;\n  bool colon = half % 2 == 0;\n  display.showNumberDecEx(shown, colon ? 0b01000000 : 0, true);\n  delay(100);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}